{"id":"8333e4d8ffbd048e","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-selberg-sieve.md","title":"Selberg Sieve","display":"df-selberg-sieve — Selberg Sieve","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-selberg-sieve","aliases":["58-df-selberg-sieve"],"display":"df-selberg-sieve — Selberg Sieve","depends_on":["[[58-df-sieve]]","[[58-df-prime-number]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-selberg-sieve"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-selberg-sieve</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-selberg-sieve — Selberg Sieve"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"03087ea1802e2ea2\" href=\"?note=03087ea1802e2ea2\" title=\"58-df-sieve\">58-df-sieve</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"58-df-prime-number\">58-df-prime-number</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in[\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}]^{&lt;\\omega}\">\\(A\\in[\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}]^{&lt;\\omega}\\)</span> (finite positive-integer set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\\subseteq\\mathbb P\">\\(P\\subseteq\\mathbb P\\)</span> (set of primes, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"58-df-prime-number\">58-df-prime-number</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"z\\in\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;1}\">\\(z\\in\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;1}\\)</span> (sieving threshold)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S(A,P,z)\\in\\omega\">\\(S(A,P,z)\\in\\omega\\)</span> (sifted-count function defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}selberg\\text{-}sieve} \\vdash A\\in[\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}]^{&lt;\\omega}\\land P\\subseteq\\mathbb P\\land z\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;1}\\to S(A,P,z)=|\\{a\\in A:\\forall p\\in P\\;(p&lt;z\\to p\\nmid a)\\}|\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}selberg\\text{-}sieve} \\vdash A\\in[\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}]^{&lt;\\omega}\\land P\\subseteq\\mathbb P\\land z\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;1}\\to S(A,P,z)=|\\{a\\in A:\\forall p\\in P\\;(p&lt;z\\to p\\nmid a)\\}|\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Selberg sieve gives upper bounds for sifted sets.</li>\n<li>Selberg weights are used to estimate this sifted count; they are not parameters of the count itself.</li>\n<li>Brun–Selberg sieve: lower bounds for sums of multiplicative functions.</li>\n<li>Rank of Selberg sieve determines quality of bound.</li>\n<li>Selberg upper-bound inequalities are downstream theorems.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-sieve","status":"resolved","id":"03087ea1802e2ea2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-sieve]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-prime-number","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-prime-number]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-prime-number","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$P\\subseteq\\mathbb P$ (set of primes, see [[58-df-prime-number]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A\\in[\\mathbb N_{>0}]^{<\\omega}","display":false},{"tex":"P\\subseteq\\mathbb P","display":false},{"tex":"z\\in\\mathbb{R}_{>1}","display":false},{"tex":"S(A,P,z)\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}selberg\\text{-}sieve} \\vdash A\\in[\\mathbb N_{>0}]^{<\\omega}\\land P\\subseteq\\mathbb P\\land z\\in\\mathbb R_{>1}\\to S(A,P,z)=|\\{a\\in A:\\forall p\\in P\\;(p<z\\to p\\nmid a)\\}|","display":true}],"bytes":1110,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1124","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-selberg-sieve.md|58-df-selberg-sieve]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["03087ea1802e2ea2","dad686059f3ca152"]}